      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): normalize local dispatch request paths",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe in-process browser route dispatcher normalized request paths differently from the node/browser proxy path. Local dispatch accepted missing leading slashes, but did not trim whitespace or strip trailing slashes the same way the shared browser request policy does.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBrowser request entry points should route and guard the same normalized path. This change reuses `normalizeBrowserRequestPath` in the local dispatcher instead of keeping a narrower local normalizer.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLocal browser request dispatch now behaves consistently with node-host browser requests for paths such as `snapshot`, `/snapshot/`, and `  snapshot/  `. Existing guarded route checks continue to use the same normalized path contract.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased cleanly onto latest `upstream/main` at `bf02b611eb`.\n- `OPENCLAW_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_SCOPE=worktree node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/dispatcher.path-normalization.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/dispatcher.abort.test.ts extensions/browser/src/node-host/invoke-browser.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose`\n  - 3 files passed, 25 tests passed.\n- `pnpm format:check extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/dispatcher.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/dispatcher.path-normalization.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n\n## Real Gateway Proof\n\nRan a real local Gateway test instance, connected over Gateway WebSocket with `operator.admin`, forced local browser dispatch with `gateway.nodes.browser.mode=off`, started the headless `openclaw` browser profile through `browser.request`, then called the actual `browser.request` handler for each raw path variant.\n\nRedacted terminal output:\n\n```json\n{\"path\":\"/start\",\"ok\":true,\"profile\":\"openclaw\"}\n{\"path\":\"snapshot\",\"ok\":true,\"format\":\"aria\",\"nodeCount\":3}\n{\"path\":\"/snapshot/\",\"ok\":true,\"format\":\"aria\",\"nodeCount\":3}\n{\"path\":\"  snapshot/  \",\"ok\":true,\"format\":\"aria\",\"nodeCount\":3}\n```\n\nThe proof exercises the real path from `browser.request` local Gateway dispatch into the browser route dispatcher and the `/snapshot` route. It does not use `openclaw browser snapshot`, because that CLI path hardcodes `/snapshot` and would not prove the raw slashless or whitespace/trailing-slash variants.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/browser-request-path-normalization",
